The two-file split is deliberate. PEFF-STYLE.md is the canonical
style reference, so the rule belongs there in full. SKILL.md step 4
is where the model is most likely to be reading when it actually sits
down to write notes, so a brief echo there reduces the chance of it
slipping through unformatted.

I considered also updating the Output Format section in SKILL.md (the
block that shows how to present notes to the user before committing),
but decided against it. That section describes the conversational notes
shown during review, not the git-stored notes. They happen to coincide
in practice, but mixing the two would blur the distinction.
